361	 *      Under the Summer Sale an $8.99 plan displayed $8.99 and took $6.29. That
362	 *      is the 2026-07-25 incident verbatim, and it is what
363	 *      test/pricing-display-vs-charge.test.ts exists to stop.
364	 *   2. It had already DRIFTED from the real order core: no `extraDiskGB`, so it
365	 *      could neither sell nor charge for the deploy-time storage upsell that
366	 *      `orderQuote` prices.
367	 *   3. It skipped two guards `placeOrder` performs — `diskCapacityCheck`, and
368	 *      the `addons.dailyBackup` -> `autoBackup`/`backupIntervalHours` bridge
369	 *      (lib/order.ts). Every server in the live DB once carried
370	 *      `addons.dailyBackup` with `autoBackup: false` and no backup job ever
371	 *      enqueued: customers paid for backups they were never going to receive.
372	 *
373	 * `payAndDeploy` below is the one deploy path. It routes through lib/order.ts —
374	 * `intentFromFormData` + `orderQuote` + `placeOrder` — and covers BOTH the
375	 * wallet-funded and the card-funded case, so nothing was lost by removing this.
376	 * If a wallet-only form is ever wanted back, it must call `placeOrder`, not
377	 * recompose the price. One formula, one charge.
